{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010971-bureaucramancy","id":1010971,"title":"Bureaucramancy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-02T01:10:25-08:00","id":1010971,"title":"Bureaucramancy","content":"So, I am designing a Mage Chronicle right now, a LARP aimed at having maybe 30 players, and a major element of it is a kind of arcane device that allows the local Assembly to vote to change certain mystical laws / local geomancy /etc. I'm looking to make democracy and politicking major themes. Problem is I find myself a little unsure of how I want the thing to work. Specifically what can actually be done with it. Here are the ideas I have in mind so far for what it can do;<ul><li>Shift local ley lines in the area, moving any number of points in Hollow between their respective sites.</li> <li>Detonate a Hollow (exact effects unknown).</li> <li>Include a new voting member.</li> <li>Expel a voting member.</li> <li>Add (or later remove) a key to certain local Iris's. The Assembly must devise and define the Key.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> I'm looking for feedback on potential problems, or other ideas about what something like this should be able to do. I'm not too worried about plausibility, since I am broadly going with 'an archmaster did it', with only minimal additional information. I was kind of hoping to have some of the functions be non-obvious, so that those functions would constitute a Mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1547-bunnirabbi","name":"BunniRabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1547_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T01:39:53-08:00","id":1010978,"title":"","content":"Other possible effects:<ul><li>Alter the resonance of a specified area via ley-line manipulation (relevant to spirit dealings).</li> <li>Attract or repel ghosts from a specified point.</li> <li>Raise or lower the strength of the Gauntlet in a targeted area.</li> <li>Create or eliminate Temenotic connections between concepts relevant to the local area, affecting Astral travel and influencing local thought patterns (e.g. maybe you create a connection between the idea of &quot;trust&quot; and the local government, inclining people to trust the local government more, or you eliminate the connections between the ideas of two neighbourhoods, causing their residents to feel more distant from one another).</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T00:43:22-08:00","id":1011403,"title":"","content":"I particularly like the ideas for changing the Gauntlet and Temenotic connections, as there are pros and cons to any change, leading to a variety of views.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1547-bunnirabbi","name":"BunniRabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1547_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T03:50:18-08:00","id":1011444,"title":"","content":"To take a cue from another game:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=970181#post970181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New York is the setting for Travis Stout's own Mage chronicle, and we've been dropping references to it since Left Hand Path.<br /> <br /> (snip) The various sub-Consilia are working on Mysteries of their own, but the big one is that Manhattan is so charged with ley energies its evolving into something. Whole city blocks move, sliding around, but the changes are subject to Quiescence so only the Awakened and Sleepwalkers are aware of it.<br /> <br /> After 9/11, Manhattan became an unexploded bomb. The Seers and Pentacle worked out a short-lived truce to deal with it, but the Seers screwed the Pentacle mages (including the Consilium's arch-Hierarch) over and somehow took control of Manhattan's Mystery. Now the island itself is hostile to Pentacle mages trying to set up shop there, so the Consilium keeps to the other Boroughs and the wider New York / New Jersey states, with some cabals raiding into Manhattan to try to figure out what's going on or recover lost treasures.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}